    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30811" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>custom, habit</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. τὸ πρόσθε τοκήων</span> (but prob. 
				f.l. for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦθος</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				728
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ σύνηθες ἔ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					894
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ τὸ ἔ. συνθήκη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Cra.</u>
					435a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πάτρια ἔ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					295a
				</span></i>
			: prov., "<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ.", φασί, "δευτέρη
			φύσις</span>" <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Mis.</u>
				353a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἔθει τῇ πόλει
			εἶναι</span> to be <i>the habit</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.64
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔ. ἐστίν τινι</span>, c.
				inf., <i><span class="en">
				Cratin.Jun.
				7.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				253
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθος ἔχειν</span>, c.
				inf., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Them.</u>
				4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔθει</span>
			<i>by habit, habitually</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φύσει</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1179b21
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ἔθει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					122
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δι᾽ ἔθος</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ γενετῆς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>EN</u>
				1154a33
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξ ἔθους</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				1103a17
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατὰ τὰ Ῥωμαίων ἔ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PSI</u>
					3.182
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A. D.)</span>, etc. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σϝέθ</span>-, cf. Lat. <i>suesco</i>; 
				v.
